        "problem": "The random variable $X$ has the following probability distribution.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.4$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ | $0.05$ | $0.05$ |\n\nLet $Y=X-4.$ Calculate $P(Y>-3).$",
        "worked_solution": "First, let's add a $Y=X-4$ row to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-4$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.4$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ | $0.05$ | $0.05$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nNow, ${f}_{X}(x)={f}_{Y}(y)$ for corresponding values of $X$ and $Y.$ Therefore, the distribution of $Y$ is as follows:\n\n| $y$ | $-4$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.4$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ | $0.05$ | $0.05$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y>-3) & =0.3+0.05+0.05 \\\\  & =0.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
